<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahom people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ahoms, Tai Ahom, Tai-Ahom</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ahom are a people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, descended from Tai followers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukaphaa">Sukaphaa</a> who entered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a> valley from upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> in 1228 and mixed with local peoples. They founded the Ahom kingdom, which ruled Assam for about six centuries. Over time they adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hinduism</a> and the Assamese language, and their chronicles, the buranjis, preserve much of the kingdom's history.</p></div>
